1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:13,740
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is November second. Japan has launched a new government agency to lead its response to disasters. Let's listen.

2
00:00:14,339 --> 00:00:17,292
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:17,992 --> 00:00:25,792
[News] 11月2日、国の新しい役所「防災庁」ができました。

4
00:00:26,492 --> 00:00:33,235
[News] 防災庁は、災害のときに国の司令塔になります。

5
00:00:33,936 --> 00:00:39,887
[News] これまでは、内閣府の中の一つの部門でした。

6
00:00:40,588 --> 00:00:48,460
[News] 働く人の数は、1.6倍の352人に増えました。

7
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:56,863
[News] 災害が起きる前の準備から、復旧や復興までを担当します。

8
00:00:57,564 --> 00:01:08,483
[News] 高市首相は、国民の命と暮らしを守ることが、国のとても大切な仕事だと話しました。

9
00:01:09,183 --> 00:01:15,784
[News] 初めての防災大臣には、細野豪志さんがなりました。

10
00:01:16,483 --> 00:01:24,140
[News] 細野大臣は、すべての国民に「緊急要請」を出しました。

11
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:30,864
[News] 家具や家電を、倒れないように固定してください。

12
00:01:31,563 --> 00:01:40,396
[News] 水や食料を、最低3日分、できれば1週間分、準備してください。

13
00:01:41,096 --> 00:01:47,816
[News] 水は、1人1日3リットル必要だと言われています。

14
00:01:48,516 --> 00:01:55,668
[News] ハザードマップを見て、避難する場所や道も確かめてください。

15
00:01:56,367 --> 00:02:06,040
[News] 防災庁は、南海トラフ地震などに備えて、地方にも拠点を作る予定です。

16
00:02:06,739 --> 00:02:08,804
[Host] Now let's break it down.

17
00:02:09,403 --> 00:02:17,756
[Slow] 11月2日、国の新しい役所「防災庁」ができました。

18
00:02:18,556 --> 00:02:25,491
[Host] On November second, a new government office, the Disaster Management Agency, was created.

19
00:02:26,092 --> 00:02:28,395
[Vocab] 防災

20
00:02:28,795 --> 00:02:31,171
[Host] It means disaster prevention.

21
00:02:31,771 --> 00:02:38,996
[Slow] 防災庁は、災害のときに国の司令塔になります。

22
00:02:39,795 --> 00:02:43,804
[Host] The agency will be the country's control tower during disasters.

23
00:02:44,403 --> 00:02:46,780
[Vocab] 災害

24
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,051
[Host] It means disaster.

25
00:02:49,651 --> 00:02:52,268
[Vocab] 司令塔

26
00:02:52,668 --> 00:02:56,075
[Host] It means control tower, or command center.

27
00:02:56,675 --> 00:03:03,036
[Slow] これまでは、内閣府の中の一つの部門でした。

28
00:03:03,836 --> 00:03:08,036
[Host] Until now, it was one section inside the Cabinet Office.

29
00:03:08,635 --> 00:03:10,675
[Vocab] 部門

30
00:03:11,075 --> 00:03:13,668
[Host] It means section or department.

31
00:03:14,268 --> 00:03:22,692
[Slow] 働く人の数は、1.6倍の352人に増えました。

32
00:03:23,491 --> 00:03:28,699
[Host] Its staff grew one point six times, to three hundred fifty-two people.

33
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,484
[Vocab] 増える

34
00:03:31,883 --> 00:03:33,804
[Host] It means to increase.

35
00:03:34,403 --> 00:03:42,659
[Slow] 災害が起きる前の準備から、復旧や復興までを担当します。

36
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:48,620
[Host] It handles everything from preparing before a disaster to recovery and rebuilding.

37
00:03:49,219 --> 00:03:51,620
[Vocab] 復旧

38
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:54,707
[Host] It means restoring things to how they were.

39
00:03:55,307 --> 00:03:58,020
[Vocab] 担当する

40
00:03:58,419 --> 00:04:00,436
[Host] It means to be in charge of.

41
00:04:01,036 --> 00:04:12,723
[Slow] 高市首相は、国民の命と暮らしを守ることが、国のとても大切な仕事だと話しました。

42
00:04:13,524 --> 00:04:20,579
[Host] Prime Minister Takaichi said protecting people's lives and daily living is a very important job for the country.

43
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:23,100
[Vocab] 命

44
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,372
[Host] It means life.

45
00:04:25,971 --> 00:04:33,028
[Slow] 初めての防災大臣には、細野豪志さんがなりました。

46
00:04:33,827 --> 00:04:37,860
[Host] Goshi Hosono became the first disaster management minister.

47
00:04:38,459 --> 00:04:40,764
[Vocab] 大臣

48
00:04:41,163 --> 00:04:43,204
[Host] It means a government minister.

49
00:04:43,803 --> 00:04:52,012
[Slow] 細野大臣は、すべての国民に「緊急要請」を出しました。

50
00:04:52,812 --> 00:04:57,540
[Host] Minister Hosono issued an emergency request to everyone in the country.

51
00:04:58,139 --> 00:05:00,516
[Vocab] 要請

52
00:05:00,915 --> 00:05:03,124
[Host] It means an official request.

53
00:05:03,723 --> 00:05:10,180
[Slow] 家具や家電を、倒れないように固定してください。

54
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:14,675
[Host] Fix your furniture and appliances so they don't fall over.

55
00:05:15,276 --> 00:05:17,795
[Vocab] 固定する

56
00:05:18,196 --> 00:05:20,740
[Host] It means to fix something in place.

57
00:05:21,339 --> 00:05:30,795
[Slow] 水や食料を、最低3日分、できれば1週間分、準備してください。

58
00:05:31,596 --> 00:05:36,803
[Host] Prepare water and food for at least three days, and if possible, one week.

59
00:05:37,403 --> 00:05:39,875
[Vocab] 食料

60
00:05:40,276 --> 00:05:42,291
[Host] It means food supplies.

61
00:05:42,891 --> 00:05:50,091
[Slow] 水は、1人1日3リットル必要だと言われています。

62
00:05:50,891 --> 00:05:54,995
[Host] It's said that one person needs three liters of water a day.

63
00:05:55,596 --> 00:05:57,995
[Vocab] 必要

64
00:05:58,396 --> 00:06:00,267
[Host] It means necessary.

65
00:06:00,867 --> 00:06:08,524
[Slow] ハザードマップを見て、避難する場所や道も確かめてください。

66
00:06:09,324 --> 00:06:13,620
[Host] Look at a hazard map and check where you would evacuate to, and the route.

67
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:16,788
[Vocab] 避難する

68
00:06:17,187 --> 00:06:19,108
[Host] It means to evacuate.

69
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:30,076
[Slow] 防災庁は、南海トラフ地震などに備えて、地方にも拠点を作る予定です。

70
00:06:30,875 --> 00:06:37,500
[Host] The agency plans to set up regional bases to prepare for big earthquakes like the Nankai Trough quake.

71
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,524
[Vocab] 備える

72
00:06:40,923 --> 00:06:43,180
[Host] It means to prepare for something.

73
00:06:43,779 --> 00:06:45,915
[Vocab] 拠点

74
00:06:46,315 --> 00:06:48,187
[Host] It means a base.

75
